{
  "_doc": "The password KDF (packages/client-core/src/crypto/kdf.ts). 'argon2id' pins the raw algorithm (RFC 9106, version 0x13, 32-byte output) that every Argon2id implementation the clients use must reproduce: the WebAssembly one on the web and the desktop app, the Bouncy Castle one on Android and @noble/hashes elsewhere. Its 'phc-*' entries are the reference implementation's own test vectors (phc-winner-argon2 src/test.c, Argon2id v1.3), with UTF-8 password and salt; 'rfc9106_argon2id' is RFC 9106 section 5.3, which also takes a secret and associated data, so only an implementation that accepts both can run it. 'derivations' pins the whole login derivation: master_key = KDF(password, salt bytes) with kdf_version 1 (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 over the password's UTF-8 bytes as given) or 2 (Argon2id over the NFC-normalized password's UTF-8 bytes); auth_hash = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = master_key, no salt, info = 'atlas-auth-v1', 32 bytes); mek = the same with info 'atlas-mek-v1'. Hex is lowercase. The 'decomposed' and 'composed' passwords are the same text in NFD and NFC form: version 2 derives the same keys from both, version 1 does not.",
